-- title:
--   Igusa presentation of the ordinary completed local ring
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q \neq 2$ and $5 \le q$, a prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, a nonzero natural number $M'$, and a commutative ring $A_0$. Assume the two equivariance clauses `hℓ` and `hM`: level-$\ell$ point data (`IsLevelPStructure`) and $\Gamma_0(p^k)$-kernel polynomials (`IsGamma0PowAt`) are carried to such data by Weierstrass variable changes, via `LevelPData.variableChange` and `kernelVariableChangeDeg` respectively. Let $\mathcal{G}$ be a family of relative group laws on the projective models of Weierstrass curves with invertible discriminant, satisfying `IsChordTangent` (each law induces addition on points over fields) and `IsOriginIdentity` (its unit section is the origin chart section with $x/y = z/y = 0$), and let $\mathcal{T}$ be a transport of raw Drinfeld pairs compatible with $\mathcal{G}$ at level $q$ satisfying `IsSectionTransport`. Let $P_0$ be a fine moduli package for the moduli datum of `rigidDataPow`, that is for the functor sending $T$ to the variable-change classes of quadruples consisting of a Weierstrass curve over $T$ with invertible discriminant, kernel polynomials for the prime powers exactly dividing $M'$, a level-$\ell$ point pair, and a Drinfeld $q$-basis; write $B_0$ for its representing $A_0$-algebra and `univ` for its universal point. Let $x$ be a raw datum over $B_0$ whose class is `univ`. Let $R$ be a Noetherian local $A_0$-algebra, complete for its maximal-ideal adic topology, with an $A_0$-algebra map $\iota : B_0 \to R$; let $k$ be a field of characteristic $q$ in which $\ell$ and $M'$ are nonzero, and $\mathrm{res}_R : R \to k$ a surjection with kernel the maximal ideal of $R$. Let $W_0$ be a complete discrete valuation domain with maximal ideal generated by $q$, with a surjection $\mathrm{res}_0 : W_0 \to k$ with kernel the maximal ideal, making $R$ a $W_0$-algebra inside a scalar tower over $A_0$ and with $\mathrm{res}_R \circ \mathrm{algebraMap} = \mathrm{res}_0$. Assume the factorisation clause `hfac`: for every Artinian local $W_0$-algebra $T$ in the tower with a residue surjection onto $k$ compatible with $\mathrm{res}_0$, every $A_0$-algebra map $\varphi : B_0 \to T$ lifting $\mathrm{res}_R \circ \iota$ extends to a unique $W_0$-algebra map $R \to T$ compatible with residues and with $\varphi$. Finally let $F_0$ be a formal group over $k$ whose power series is the formal group law `formalGroupLawFixed` of the curve carried by the Drinfeld-pair component of the datum obtained from $x$ by transport along $\iota$ and reduction along $\mathrm{res}_R$, and assume the ordinarity hypothesis that $F_0$'s $q$-th iterated series `nthSeries q` equals $u \cdot X^q$ for some unit $u$ in $k[[X]]$. The conclusion is that there exists a monic polynomial $g$ over $W_0[[t]]$ of degree $q-1$ whose coefficients in degrees $< q-1$ lie in the maximal ideal of $W_0[[t]]$ and whose constant coefficient is $q$ times a unit, together with an isomorphism of $W_0$-algebras $R \cong W_0[[t]][X]/(g)$.
--
--   This is the Igusa-type local structure theorem for the ordinary locus of the Katz–Mazur moduli problem with $\Gamma_0(M') \times \Gamma(\ell) \times$ Drinfeld-$\Gamma(q)$ level: under ordinarity of the reduced formal group, the completed local ring of the fine moduli package is an Eisenstein extension of degree $q-1$ of $W_0[[t]]$. It feeds the normality and reducedness statements for the completed ordinary stalk used in the full-level analysis, namely [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.isDomain_and_isIntegrallyClosed_adicCompletion_of_nthSeries_eq_mul_X_pow_levelModuliPackageAbs_gamma0Pow`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.isDomain_and_isIntegrallyClosed_adicCompletion_of_nthSeries_eq_mul_X_pow_levelModuliPackageAbs_gamma0Pow) and [`ModularCurve.LevelModuliPackageAbs.isReduced_quotient_span_one_sub_of_pow_eq_one_of_factorsThrough_of_nthSeries_eq_mul_X_pow_gamma0Pow`](thm.html#ModularCurve.LevelModuliPackageAbs.isReduced_quotient_span_one_sub_of_pow_eq_one_of_factorsThrough_of_nthSeries_eq_mul_X_pow_gamma0Pow).
